\label{cor:universal-X}
The deformation family $\widehat\pi$ is formally universal for
$\operatorname{Def}_m^X$.

\label{prop:decomposition-family}
The assignment defines a graded homomorphism
$\psi_{\mathcal D}^*:B_0\to\mathbb C[\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_k]$.
The pullback of the pair family along
$\psi_{\mathcal D}:\mathbb A^k\to\operatorname{Spec} B_0$ is flat, with multiplication
\begin{equation}\label{eq:decomposition-family}
 e_ce_d=\prod_{i=1}^k(U-\lambda_i)^ 
 {\eta_{i,\mathbb Z}(c)+\eta_{i,\mathbb Z}(d)-\eta_{i,\mathbb Z}(c+d)}e_{c+d}.
\end{equation}

\label{lem:truncationcohomology}
For every $j\ge1$, restriction of homogeneous Harrison cochains induces
isomorphisms
\begin{equation}\label{eq:truncationcohomology}
 T_{X_\tau}^i(-jm)\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }T_{X_\sigma}^i(-jm),
 \qquad i=1,2.
\end{equation}
These are the tangent and obstruction maps associated to $\mathcal R$.
